                    </span>

            </div>


    <div>&nbsp;</div>
    <div class="component comp-footnotes" data-component="Footnotes">

                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote1" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 1"><sup>1</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>I am grateful to Roy Webb and John Weinberg for assistance in preparing these remarks.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote2" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 2"><sup>2</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, "Are Recoveries from Banking and Financial Crises Really So Different?"&nbsp;International Finance Discussion Papers, no. 1037, November 2011.&nbsp; See in particular Figure 12, page 24.&nbsp; The current recovery is within one standard error of the average advanced economy recovery from recessions that occur during housing slumps.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote3" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 3"><sup>3</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, “<a href="http://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/press/monetary/20120125c.htm">Longer-Run Goals and Policy Strategy</a>.” News and Events, Monetary Policy Press Release, January 25, 2012.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-footnotes__note">
                    <a href="javascript:;" id="footnote4" class="comp-footnotes__note-num" aria-label="Go to inline footnote 4"><sup>4</sup></a>
                    <div class="comp-footnotes__content"><p>Jeffrey M. Lacker, “<a href="/press_room/speeches/jeffrey_m_lacker/2012/lacker_speech_20121120">Perspectives on Monetary and Credit Policy</a>.” Speech at the Shadow Open Market Committee Symposium, New York, November 20, 2012.</p></div>
                </div>
    </div>
